      "parent_visual": {
        "decision": "Bounded pass for an embroidery-inspired stylized candidate, explicitly retaining ambiguous diamond reading and weak mobile textile detail; not an authentic-pattern or thread-realism approval.",
        "hardware": "Brass clasp/corner caps and side ring present; front metal blends somewhat with honey wood. Open latch separation is intentional; rear hinge details remain small. Gray irregular feet are visible.",
        "limitations": "Frozen still-image review only; supplied technical passes were not rerun. No final user approval, photoreal equivalence, physical-phone performance, cultural authentication or continuous mechanical certification. Open disengaged latch is expected; hidden exterior lid ornament in open views is not missing. Invented arrangement is not authenticated regional embroidery; wood/brass are family choices. Surface-mounted rather than recessed panel and noisy historical source poster are documented limitations.",
        "quality": "Warm wooden shell, dark bordered stitch panel and red geometric accents are clear; open cavity and full silhouette fit both viewports. Marketing broadly preserves the actual composition.",
        "terrain": "Not applicable: raised stitch motif on a surface-mounted dark plaque. At oblique/mobile scale the three intended diamonds read as stepped or linked rectangular outlines rather than distinctly separated diamonds; marketing also reads as linked stepped rectangles.",
        "texture": "Actual wood grain reads evenly patterned; charcoal weave and individual thread twist/penetration are unresolved. Crimson relief appears regular, relatively flat and sometimes coral. Marketing is cleaner and more tactile but not proof of real embroidery."
      },
